FIT
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The FIT protocol and FIT file format are proprietary to Garmin.  This project
reads FIT files through fitactivity, which uses an independent third-party Go
implementation (github.com/muktihari/fit), and neither includes nor
distributes any part of Garmin's FIT SDK.  This project is not affiliated with
or endorsed by Garmin.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Data
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

course ships no map data and contacts no map service.  It reads a store the
user filled with osmbase, and the data in that store carries its own terms,
which attach to what course prints from it.

OpenStreetMap              Map data is (c) OpenStreetMap contributors,
                           available under the Open Database License (ODbL).
                           A place name read from it is a Produced Work, so
                           the credit must travel with it; share-alike does
                           not reach it.  course prints the credit the store's
                           manifest records -- never a constant -- beside
                           every summary that named a place from the tiles,
                           and writes it into the JSON and YAML documents, so
                           it goes wherever the answer is pasted.

Natural Earth              Country, region and sea outlines.  Public domain;
                           credited anyway, per answer, so a reader can tell
                           two names in one summary came from different
                           places under different terms.
